# Legacy redirects from the old staykeep.com (Next.js) site. Cloudflare's
# static-asset layer (the `ASSETS` binding in wrangler.toml) evaluates this
# file directly — see worker/index.ts for the one thing it does NOT cover
# (the www -> apex host redirect, which needs the Worker itself).
#
# Cloudflare's `_redirects` only supports a trailing `*` wildcard, matched
# back with `:splat` — no mid-path named placeholders — hence `/*` + `:splat`
# below rather than `/:id`. Exact-match rules are listed before the
# wildcard ones per wrangler's own ordering hint (plain rules are cheaper to
# match than splat/placeholder ones) — this is a performance note only, none
# of these rules overlap so the order never changes what matches.
#
# Never add a rule that matches `/.well-known/*` or `/apple-app-site-association`
# here — those two files must be served directly, never redirected.

/profile      https://app.staykeep.com/account            301
/inbox        https://app.staykeep.com/trips              301
/features     /owners   301
/manage       /owners   301
/pricing      /owners   301

# The old blog (app/blog) had four placeholder posts with fabricated
# stats/dates, not real content — see the handoff report. Nothing worth
# porting, so it redirects home rather than to /owners.
/blog         /   301

/property/*   https://app.staykeep.com/property/:splat   301
/booking/*    https://app.staykeep.com/trips/:splat       301
/profile/*    https://app.staykeep.com/account            301
/inbox/*      https://app.staykeep.com/trips              301
/features/*   /owners   301
/blog/*       /   301
